COVID. Does it work to require incoming travelers&nbsp;
to test? Well, we'll talk about that in a moment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:30.780
NPR reports. U.S. will require travelers from&nbsp;
China to show negative COVID tests before flight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:38.280
This will apply to travelers from China, Hong Kong&nbsp;
and Macao to show a negative COVID test before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:43.200
entering the United States. The CDC announced the&nbsp;
measure yesterday. It will go into effect January&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:49.800
five for all passengers over age two. Passengers&nbsp;
must show a negative PCR or monitored antigen test&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:53.880
no more than two days before departure. Whether&nbsp;
it's a direct flight or whether you're coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:59.520
from another country, if you go China, London, New&nbsp;
York, you would still have to show such a test,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:03.900
even though, strictly speaking, your flight is&nbsp;
coming into the U.S.. From London, the monitor&nbsp;&nbsp;

