spread? Yes. I mean, the idea makes some sense.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:40.080
The difficulties are many, the supervised antigen&nbsp;
tests. Remember when I was in Spain last summer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:45.060
my girlfriend that I did these supervised&nbsp;
antigen tests where it's just a home test,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:51.060
but someone watches you do it. And my girlfriend&nbsp;
got two false positives and she was negative. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:57.240
ended up having to find a hospital on a Sunday&nbsp;
Catholic holiday in Spain, which I can tell you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.240 --> 00:04:01.800
is very difficult to do. Get a PCR. Turned&nbsp;
out she was. It turned out she was negative.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:07.860
Those tests are not the most accurate. But&nbsp;
not only are false positives a problem,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:12.300
false negatives, particularly in asymptomatic&nbsp;
people, are a major, major problem. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:18.060
when I had COVID a few weeks ago, I was testing&nbsp;
negative on those tests, even though I had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:24.120
COVID until I don't even know, I guess, day&nbsp;
three of my symptoms. So the limitations are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:32.340
asymptomatic. People often test negative on those&nbsp;
tests. It's not a guarantee you're not infected.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:37.560
The fact that you can get the test two&nbsp;
days before travel makes it particularly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:42.600
unhelpful. The incubation period of COVID, even&nbsp;
though, you know, if you look at the bell curve,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:47.940
most people start showing symptoms between 2 to 5&nbsp;
days after exposure. It can be up to ten or even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:55.080
more days. So is that a reason not to do anything?&nbsp;
No, but it is a reason why the technique may not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.080 --> 00:05:00.360
be that effective. To be perfectly frank,&nbsp;
the most effective part of requiring testing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:05.940
